    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="1221" n="1159" sameAs="frus:frus1945v01/pg1159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/6–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the United States Delegation</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stettinius</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Francisco</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-05">June 5,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received June 5—9:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Will you be good enough to transmit the following to the President: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Soviet Ambassador yesterday afternoon told me that his Government
                            had instructed him to inform me that it favored the permanent seat of
                            the new international organization being located in the United States. I
                            thanked the Ambassador for this thought on behalf of the Soviet
                            Government but explained, that our thinking had been along the line of
                            the location being in an internationalized district of some type and not
                            directly within the territory of any sovereign <pb facs="1222" n="1160"
                                xml:id="pg1160"/> member state of the organization. I explained that
                            had been President Roosevelt’s thinking but that I
                            would inform you of this suggestion of the Soviet Government in order
                            that you could consider the question.</p>
                        <p>It is a matter, however, on which decision can be deferred until after
                            the San Francisco, Conference. It is a matter to which the preparatory
                            commission for the new organization can give study.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                        
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
